    "details": {
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><strong>Deathrattle Skeletons.</strong> This warrior of Vyrkos Dynasty enters the field with a complete D&D 5e profile: armor, hit points, weapons, racial traits, and tactical maneuvers are all resolved directly from the embedded items on this actor. Its battlefield presence is practical rather than ornamental: auras name their radius, diseases name their saving throws, and maneuvers state their action economy.</p><p>Use the inventory as the creature’s tactical menu. Weapons list finished attack or saving throw text; features describe the exact condition, movement, advantage, damage, recharge, or aura they create.</p><blockquote><p>“A wolf does not ask the forest for permission to hunt.”<br><em>— Belladamma Volga</em></p></blockquote><p><strong>Wargear and battlefield powers.</strong> This creature enters battle with Wolf Claws, Moonlit Sabre, Hunting Spear, Vyrkos Wolf-Blood, Claws of the Vyrkos Pack, Wolf Fang Blade, Necromantic Undead, Deathless Will. Its drilled responses, charms, blades, and battlefield rites shape the rhythm of its turns.</p>",
